        {
          "field": "stem",
          "before": null,
          "after": "Let \\(f(x)\\) be a polynomial with \\(f(2)=-6\\). Which expression must have the factor \\(2x+1\\)?"
        },
        {
          "field": "stemZh",
          "before": null,
          "after": "設 \\(f(x)\\) 為多項式，且 \\(f(2)=-6\\)。下列哪個式子必定有因式 \\(2x+1\\)？"
        },
        {
          "field": "solution",
          "before": null,
          "after": "Set \\(x=-\\frac12\\). Then \\(2x+3=2\\), so \\[\\begin{gathered}f(2x+3) +6 =f(2) +6 \\\\ =0\\end{gathered}\\] By the factor theorem, option D has the factor \\(2x+1\\). The other choices need information about \\(f(0)\\) or give \\(-12\\)."
        },
        {
          "field": "solutionZh",
          "before": null,
          "after": "代入 \\(x=-\\frac12\\)，得 \\(2x+3=2\\)，所以 \\[\\begin{gathered}f(2x+3) +6 =f(2) +6 \\\\ =0\\end{gathered}\\]由因式定理，D 必有因式 \\(2x+1\\)。其他選項須知道 \\(f(0)\\) 或得到 \\(-12\\)。"
        },
        {
          "field": "solutionStatus",
          "before": null,
          "after": "independently-rederived"
